{Tactics that serve a positional goal: use pins to win back material and free your game.
Tal as Black in a Modern Benoni, the most dynamic answer to 1.d4.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3.
Nc3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. e4 g6 7. Be2 Bg7 8. Nf3 O-O 9. O-O Re8 10. Qc2 Na6 11. Bf4
Nb4 12. Qb1 Nxe4 {Question: White's e4 pawn looks protected. Is it? A pseudo-sacrifice.
13.Nxe4 Bf5 pins the knight to the queen on b1, and with ...Nxd5 next Black wins the
material back and frees his game. The engine calls it equal and active.} 13. Nxe4 Bf5 14.
Nfd2 Nxd5 15. Bxd6 Nf6 16. Bf3 Nxe4 17. Nxe4 Bxe4 18. Bxe4 Qxd6 19. Qc2 Re7 20. Bf3 Rae8
21. Rad1 Bd4 22. a4 b6 23. b3 Re5 24. Rd2 h5 25. Re2 Rxe2 26. Bxe2 h4 27. Kh1 Qf4 28. g3
Qf6 29. Qd1 Rd8 30. Bg4 Bxf2 {Another strike at f2. White's king is exposed and Black's
rook gets into d2 (engine about +2).} 31. Qe2 Rd2 32. Qe8+ Kg7 33. gxh4 Qd4 34. Bh3 Qd3
35. Bg2 Rd1 {White resigned.} 0-1

[Event "Tal – Simagin, USSR Championship 1956"]
[White "Tal"]
[Black "Simagin"]
[Date "1956.??.??"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Annotator "KNIGHT'nMARE coach notes (engine-checked with Stockfish)"]

{Drag the king into the open, then hunt it with checks. Afterwards, check your sacrifices.
Young Tal against a solid defence. Black's king stays in the centre a move too long.} 1.
e4 c6 2. d4 d6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f4 Qb6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Be2 Nbd7 7. e5 {Space with tempo against
the f6 knight.} 7... Nd5 8. O-O Nxc3 9. bxc3 e6 10. Ng5 Bxe2 11. Qxe2 h6 12. Nxf7
{Question: Black's king is still in the centre. Can you sacrifice to open it? A knight
sacrifice to drag the king out. The engine actually prefers 12.Qh5 (about +1.7), but after
12...Kxf7 13.f5 lines open at once and Black has to defend accurately for many moves.}
12... Kxf7 13. f5 dxe5 14. fxe6+ Kxe6 15. Rb1 {Tal offers a rook to deflect the black
queen. After 15...Qxb1 16.Qc4+, queen and bishop hunt the king. The engine prefers 15.Be3,
but this still wins.} 15... Qxb1 16. Qc4+ Kd6 17. Ba3+ Kc7 18. Rxb1 Bxa3 19. Qb3 Be7 20.
Qxb7+ Kd6 21. dxe5+ Nxe5 22. Rd1+ Ke6 23. Qb3+ Kf5 24. Rf1+ Ke4 25. Re1+ Kf5 26. g4+ Kf6
27. Rf1+ Kg6 28. Qe6+ Kh7 29. Qxe5 Rhe8 30. Rf7 Bf8 31. Qf5+ Kg8 32. Kf2 Bc5+ 33. Kg3 Re3+
34. Kh4 Rae8 35. Rxg7+ {The final blow. White soon queens a pawn.} 35... Kxg7 36. Qxc5
R8e6 37. Qxa7+ Kg6 38. Qa8 Kf6 39. a4 Ke5 40. a5 Kd5 41. Qd8+ Ke4 42. a6 Kf3 43. a7 Re2
44. Qd3+ R2e3 45. Qxe3+ 1-0
